{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/56270-question-about-the-sixth-maelstrom-what-officially-caused-it","id":56270,"title":"question about the Sixth Maelstrom....what officially caused it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-23T12:01:31-08:00","id":56270,"title":"question about the Sixth Maelstrom....what officially caused it?","content":"Ok..on the canon of wraith (SPOILERS), they mention that a nuke was send down to the oblivion and that caused it....But also we know that the killing of Ravnos by the Technocracy caused the maelstrom..so...which one is the oficial version?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T12:47:48-08:00","id":56293,"title":"","content":"I could be wrong but<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">the nuke are 3-4 in a short time<br /> the first sent on the spiritual Enoch in the Tempest by the Deathlords of Stygia<br /> the second sent in the Oblivion Mouth by a member of the Orphic Circle,<br /> and this is the first stage of the Maelstrom<br /> then Ravana rises, IT begin drinking Methuselah and hatch a massive battle in the north Bangladesh by IT, local Garou and maybe other shapeshifters, Technocracy SWAT, Cathayans, phantoms created by Ravana and others<br /> the the Technocracy nuke Ravana, 1 or 2 times (I don't remember), in the end it dies thanks to the sun, but in the short time of a couple days over 200.000 people are dead, thanks to the battle.<br /> The last nuke (or nukes), and the thousand souls siphoned in the Shadowland / Oblivion, give the still rising Maelstrom its spin</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T12:56:58-08:00","id":56300,"title":"","content":"The Week of Nightmares didn't cause the 6GM but it did help weaken things in the Underworld. People tend to think one created the other because they happened in close proximity to each other.<br /> <br /> Anyway the 6GM was ultimately cause the detonation of the relics of Fat Man and Little Boy*. The first was detonated by the Hierarchy (probably the Smiling Lord's doing) on Enoch** while at the same Xerxes Jones, a VE working for the Orphic Circle was in the Labyrinth with the second, planning to detonate it in mouth of Oblivion. Despite what some think Jones didn't trigger his, it went off when the shockwave from the first nuke hit Jones's ship.<br /> <br /> *At least I believe it was Fat Man and Little Boy but I can't remember where I read that right now. But given the effects those two bombs had on Japan, slowing tainting the chi of the entire island and devastating the Shadowlands of those two cities, it would be fitting.<br /> <br /> **Basically Anubis called in a favor the Ferrymen owed him and they manipulated the Hierarchy into invading Enoch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T13:38:11-08:00","id":56333,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">In <i>Book of Legions</i>, I believe the Smiling Lord comments about having agents at Los Alamos who were turning nukes into relics after their test detonations. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T13:46:13-08:00","id":56340,"title":"","content":"Chi-tainting is an aspect that is a tad incongruous with the rampant nuclear testing of the Cold War and tensions between India and Pakistan. Especially since the terrain typically chosen for such sites was usually the kind of place where a caern would be (isolated wilderness that few humans lived in). I could see death-taint on account of the Nihils that were created, but if Zmei Goluko can survive a number of impacts from Russian thermonuclear weapons (admittedly not well) and Russia has more to fear from his brethren eating caerns than having them poisoned, some other pieces are needed to make that picture come together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T14:14:08-08:00","id":56358,"title":"","content":"Actually I believe the chi-tainting was caused by combination of all those sudden deaths, the terrible suffering of the survivors and the radiation. If you take a look at the Dark Kingdom of Jade Adventures book, one of the chapters deals with the PCs doing to Hiroshima (I think I can't remember, but it is one of the two cities) and the Shadowlands of that place is... well its a place sane wraiths don't go without a <i>very</i> good reason.<br /> <br /> Nuking some remote stretch of nowhere won't do as much damage as nukes being dropped on two cities with thousands of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T14:28:43-08:00","id":56364,"title":"","content":"Official version is in <i>Ends of Empire</i>. To sum up:<br /> <br /> -Xerxes Jones, a techno-mage of some sort, travels to the Well of Oblivion, basically the center of the Labyrinth, with the intent of detonating a nuke in the Well to see what happens (because SCIENCE!),<br /> -At the same time, the Smiling Lord and the Legions of Stygia invade and besiege Enoch. To wipe out the vampires, the Smiling Lord drops a relic nuke on the city (Fat Man, iirc). He keeps the other relic nuke (Little Boy) in reserve, possibly (most definitely) to use against Yu Haung and the Jade Empire.<br /> -The shock-wave from Enoch's destruction reverbrates through the Underworld, causing smaller storms. It travels down through the Labyrinth, triggering and detonating Xerxes Jones' own device. His magic-nuke goes off in the Labyrinth, causing Oblivion to explode outward. At this point they are just two Maelstroms.<br /> -Like two storm fronts, because that's basically what they are, these two events meet and feed into each other. They are on the verge of becoming a Great Maelstrom.<br /> -Depending on your view of canon, the Week of Nightmares happens now; the excessive and sudden death toll gives the (almost) Great Maelstrom in the Underworld that little extra push it needed, and it becomes<b> <i>The Sixth Great Maelstrom</i></b> (emphasis added for extra gravitas).<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T15:09:57-08:00","id":331512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/56270-question-about-the-sixth-maelstrom-what-officially-caused-it?p=56364#post56364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Official version is in <i>Ends of Empire</i>. To sum up:<br /> <br /> <br /> -At the same time, the Smiling Lord and the Legions of Stygia invade and besiege Enoch. To wipe out the vampires, the Smiling Lord drops a relic nuke on the city (Fat Man, iirc). He keeps the other relic nuke (Little Boy) in reserve, possibly (most definitely) to use against Yu Haung and the Jade Empire.<br /> <br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC, 'Little Boy' is suppose to be with the Malefean Pika-Don (as per DKoJ) in it's pit; I'm not sure as to the fate of 'Fat Man' but I believe that EoE specifically states somewhere that it was the Relic of 'Trinity' (the 1st of the Los Alamos test shots) that was dropped on Enoch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is the Line of Division...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3797-terminus-est","name":"Terminus Est","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3797_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}